    <description>On Trade-In (Appraisal) creation, assigns a follow-up Task to the initiating Sales Rep (AF_InitiatingSalesRep__c, or their Manager if the Rep is inactive). If AF_InitiatingSalesRep__c is blank (e.g. API insert, or a creation path that never populates it), the Task owner defaults to the Appraisal&apos;s own OwnerId instead of being left blank — this prevents the Task DML from failing with a required-owner error and rolling back the whole Appraisal transaction (LFRDN-629). 2 business days later (placeholder timeframe pending business confirmation), if the outcome is still not recorded, escalates by creating a follow-up Task for the initiating Rep&apos;s Manager (acting as Showroom Manager proxy via the management hierarchy), also defaulting to the Appraisal&apos;s OwnerId if the initiating rep can&apos;t be resolved. Deliberately keyed off AF_InitiatingSalesRep__c rather than OwnerId as the primary source — OwnerId is reassigned to the AF_Q_UsedCarTeam queue once the trade-in is submitted for evaluation (a queue has no IsActive/ManagerId), so it can&apos;t stand in for &quot;the rep who initiated this&quot; as the primary signal, but it is always populated and safe as a fallback so the flow never fails the transaction.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
